2. Permitted use

You may view, download, run, copy and adapt Cermes for your own use free of
charge. This includes using it as a checkout system in associations and
businesses. Goods or services whose sales are recorded using Cermes may be
sold. The resulting revenue belongs to the respective operator.

You may distribute Cermes and modified versions free of charge if you
include the source code of the distributed version, this license and the
existing copyright notices. Changes must be identified as such. These
license terms must remain in effect for the reused and modified Cermes
components. You may not impose additional restrictions on the free use
permitted here.

3. No sale and no paid offering

Without prior express permission from Yakub Uyar, you may not sell Cermes
or versions based on it, license or distribute them for a fee, or offer
them as a paid software service. You may not charge for downloading,
accessing or using the software. This prohibition also applies to modified
versions and to including Cermes components in paid software offerings.

Selling goods or services whose sales are merely recorded using Cermes
does not fall under this prohibition.

4. Operator responsibility, warranty and liability

Use is at your own risk. Cermes is provided free of charge, as is, without
warranty, any commitment to provide support, or any maintenance obligation,
to the extent permitted by law.

Before production use, operators must review the code and application for
suitability, correct operation, security, data protection, and the legal
requirements applicable to their intended use. Operators are responsible
for operation, access permissions and backups. No suitability or legal
compliance for a particular purpose is warranted.

To the extent permitted by law, no liability is accepted for damage arising
from use or inability to use the software. Liability imposed by mandatory
law, in particular for intentional misconduct and any other liability that
cannot legally be excluded, remains unaffected.

5. Other rights and language versions

No further usage rights are granted by this license. Mandatory statutory
rights remain unaffected. Any exceptions require an express agreement
with Yakub Uyar.

The English version is provided for readability. If the language versions
differ, the German version prevails to the extent legally permissible.
